    "theorem": "JVGradedHilbertAudit.canonical_graded_hilbert_certificate",
    "statement": "theorem canonical_graded_hilbert_certificate : Ideal.IsHomogeneous sourceGrading JVMacaulayAudit.sourceIdeal ∧ (∀ d : ℕ, ∀ p : sourceGrading d, p ∈ LinearMap.ker (degreeMap d) ↔ (p : Poly) ∈ JVMacaulayAudit.sourceIdeal) ∧ (∀ d : ℕ, Nonempty (degreePiece d ≃ₗ[F] degreeImage d)) ∧ (∀ d : ℕ, degreeImage d = gradedSpan d) ∧ (∀ d : ℕ, hilbertFunction d = if d = 0 then 1 else if d = 1 then 3 else if d = 2 then 3 else if d = 3 then 1 else 0) ∧ (hilbertFunction 0 = 1 ∧ hilbertFunction 1 = 3 ∧ hilbertFunction 2 = 3 ∧ hilbertFunction 3 = 1) ∧ (∀ d : ℕ, 4 ≤ d → hilbertFunction d = 0) ∧ (∀ d : ℕ, hilbertFunction d = 0 ↔ 4 ≤ d) ∧ Module.finrank F A = 8 ∧ Module.length F A = 8 ∧ hilbertFunction 0 ≠ Module.finrank F A",
    "decl_sha256": "288fa232f61b729eee2a64e17f2741efcf7c144c019684d0bc676e5fcd2db8b6",
    "scope": "Actual canonical graded pieces of the frozen first literal Joux–Vitse homogeneous F101 source ideal I in P=F101[x,y,h]. Proves I is homogeneous for Mathlib standard grading. DegreeMap is the actual quotient map P→P/I restricted to Mathlib degree-d homogeneous submodule; its kernel is exactly I intersected with that domain. Canonical piece P_d/ker(DegreeMap) is linearly equivalent to its actual image; image equals span of precisely matching-degree vectors of the previously proved actual quotient basis, derived from checked actual multiplication tables and monomial/homogeneous induction. Exact canonical degree-piece dimensions1,3,3,1,0 thereafter, zero iff d≥4; total scalar dimension/length8 retained and direct graded-dimension-versus-total-dimension inequality. No ideal-homogeneity/basis/Hilbert/GB/regularity/native-output conclusion is supplied as a premise; unchanged old actual-object proof reused. Closes the finite canonical per-degree identification, not generic JV Assumption2, FGHR genericity/n≥3, internalF4 degree/refinement, whole-curve order/scalar relations or a general graded-module Hilbert polynomial theory. Mathematical source and prior work credited, no novelty or qualified-source refutation. Independent native written-header check is procedural, not kernel parser/hash/execution refinement. Standard foundations/default settings; no holes/custom axioms/native proof evaluation/global flags/raised limits/waivers/new cryptographic experiment/paid compute/agent upload.",
